tate = check_random_state(0)\n14 |     one_core = []\n15 |     multi_core = []\n16 |     sample_sizes = range(1000, 6000, 1000)\n17 | \n18 |     for n_samples in sample_sizes:\n19 |         X = random_state.rand(n_samples, 300)\n20 | \n21 |         start = time.time()\n22 |         func(X, n_jobs=1)\n23 |         one_core.append(time.time() - start)\n24 | \n25 |         start = time.time()\n26 |         func(X, n_jobs=-1)\n27 |         multi_core.append(time.time() - start)\n28 | \n29 |     plt.figure(\"scikit-learn parallel %s benchmark results\" % func.__name__)\n30 |     plt.plot(sample_sizes, one_core, label=\"one core\")\n31 |     plt.plot(sample_sizes, multi_core, label=\"multi core\")\n32 |     plt.xlabel(\"n_samples\")\n33 |     plt.ylabel(\"Time (s)\")\n34 |     plt.title(\"Parallel %s\" % func.__name__)\n35 |     plt.legend()\n```\n\n\n\n##Searching for term \"CalibrationDisplay.from_estimator\"...\n### Search Result:\nFound function `sklearn/metrics/_plot/det_curve.py:DetCurveDisplay.from_estimator`.\nSource: Match found for entity name `from_estimator`.\n```\n 84 | def from_estimator(\n 85 |         cls,\n 86 |         estimator,\n 87 |         X,\n 88 |         y,\n 89 |         *,\n 90 |         sample_weight=None,\n 91 |         response_method=\"auto\",\n 92 |         pos_label=None,\n 93 |         name=None,\n 94 |         ax=None,\n 95 |         **kwargs,\n 96 |     ):\n 97 |         \"\"\"Plot DET curve given an estimator and data.\n 98 | \n 99 |         Read more in the :ref:`User Guide <visualizations>`.\n100 | \n101 |         .. versionadded:: 1.0\n102 | \n103 |         Parameters\n104 |         ----------\n105 |         estimator : estimator instance\n106 |             Fitted classifier or a fitted :class:`~sklearn.pipeline.Pipeline`\n107 |             in which the last estimator is a classifier.\n108 | \n109 |         X : {array-like, sparse matrix} of shape (n_samples, n_features)\n110 |             Input values.\n111 | \n112 |         y : a