et with alpha=0.6\n76 |             bar.set_facecolor(color)\n77 | \n78 |         ax.tick_params(labelbottom=False, labeltop=False,\n79 |                        labelleft=False, labelright=False)\n80 | \n81 |         ax.grid(lw=lw_grid, color='0.9')\n82 |         ax.set_rmax(9)\n83 |         ax.set_yticks(rgrid)\n84 | \n85 |         # the actual visible background - extends a bit beyond the axis\n86 |         ax.add_patch(Rectangle((0, 0), arc, 9.58,\n87 |                                facecolor='white', zorder=0,\n88 |                                clip_on=False, in_layout=False))\n89 |         return ax\n```\n"}, {"content": "```\nlib/matplotlib/axes/_axes.py\nfunction: bar\n\nlib/matplotlib/patches.py\nclass: Rectangle\nfunction: set_facecolor\n\nlib/matplotlib/axes/_axes.py\nfunction: hist\n\ngalleries/examples/misc/logos2.py\nfunction: create_icon_axes\n\nlib/mpl_toolkits/mplot3d/axes3d.py\nfunction: bar3d\n```", "role": "assistant", "tool_calls": null, "function_call": null}, {"role": "user", "content": "Verify if the found locations contain all the necessary information to address the issue, and check for any relevant references in other parts of the codebase that may not have appeared in the search results. If not, continue searching for additional locations related to the issue.\nVerify that you have carefully analyzed the impact of the found locations on the repository, especially their dependencies. If you think you have solved the task, rewrite your final answer into the required location-only format, output ONLY the location block, and then call `finish` to finish.\nIMPORTANT: YOU SHOULD NEVER ASK FOR HUMAN HELP.\n"}, {"content": "<function=search_code_snippets>\n<parameter=search_terms>\n[\"facecolor accept sequence\", \"facecolor parameter precedence\", \"scatter c parameter\"]\n</parameter>\n", "role": "assistant", "tool_calls": null, "function_call": null}, {"role": "tool", "tool_call_id": "toolu_01", "name": "search_code_snippets", "content": "OB