ted arguments of `.Axes.scatter`.\n4543 | \n4544 |         Argument precedence for facecolors:\n4545 | \n4546 |         - c (if not None)\n4547 |         - kwargs['facecolor']\n4548 |         - kwargs['facecolors']\n4549 |         - kwargs['color'] (==kwcolor)\n4550 |         - 'b' if in classic mode else the result of ``get_next_color_func()``\n4551 | \n4552 |         Argument precedence for edgecolors:\n4553 | \n4554 |         - kwargs['edgecolor']\n4555 |         - edgecolors (is an explicit kw argument in scatter())\n4556 |         - kwargs['color'] (==kwcolor)\n4557 |         - 'face' if not in classic mode else None\n4558 | \n4559 |         Parameters\n4560 |         ----------\n4561 |         c : :mpltype:`color` or array-like or list of :mpltype:`color` or None\n4562 |             See argument description of `.Axes.scatter`.\n4563 |         edgecolors : :mpltype:`color` or sequence of color or {'face', 'none'} or None\n4564 |             See argument description of `.Axes.scatter`.\n4565 |         kwargs : dict\n4566 |             Additional kwargs. If these keys exist, we pop and process them:\n4567 |             'facecolors', 'facecolor', 'edgecolor', 'color'\n4568 |             Note: The dict is modified by this function.\n4569 |         xsize : int\n4570 |             The size of the x and y arrays passed to `.Axes.scatter`.\n4571 |         get_next_color_func : callable\n4572 |             A callable that returns a color. This color is used as facecolor\n4573 |             if no other color is provided.\n4574 | \n4575 |             Note, that this is a function rather than a fixed color value to\n4576 |             support conditional evaluation of the next color.  As of the\n4577 |             current implementation obtaining the next color from the\n4578 |             property cycle advances the cycle. This must only happen if we\n4579 |             actually use the color, which will only be decided within this\n4580 |             method.\n4581 | \n45